    "profile_text": {
        "body": "AeroVironment, which refers to itself as AV, describes itself as a manufacturer of unmanned aircraft systems, unmanned aerial vehicles, loitering munition systems, and unmanned ground vehicles used for surveillance and reconnaissance by the United States military, U.S. allies, and commercial industries. The company also says it manufactures high-altitude pseudo-satellites.\n\nIts advanced development group, MacCready Works, is described as turning concepts into mission-ready autonomous systems. The company says the group is named for the pioneering spirit of Dr. Paul B. MacCready, Jr., and that its engineers, roboticists, and AI researchers design next-generation robotic systems across air, land, and sea. It describes its approach as the MacCready Method, summarized on the site as build fast, test relentlessly, deploy advantage, with small multidisciplinary teams moving ideas into operational capability in months.\n\nThe company is a public company traded under the ticker AVAV, with CIK 0001368622, headquartered in Arlington, Virginia. Its recorded legal exposure is in Virginia, with 152 entries. The record lists no individual products and no MCP servers for the company.",
